C0004.description:
Spec §3A (line 94) and §3B (lines 96-97) are jointly unsatisfiable for the input class §3B exists to serve. §3A requires `report.py` to "Require and consume the `summary`-based structure"; §3B requires mapping legacy fit key `p` → `estimated_p`. But legacy `p` is produced by legacy `evaluate.py`, whose documents have no `summary` — and `report.py:71-80` gates `_normalise_fit` *behind* the summary check, raising `ValueError` first. Executed:
legacy document  {"corroboration_fit":{"p":0.42,...}, no summary}
  -> RC=1  "Error: evaluation JSON missing expected report schema"   (mapping never runs)
new schema + legacy fit key {"summary":{...}, "corroboration_fit":{"p":0.42}}
  -> RC=0  "Estimated p:  0.4200"                                    (mapping runs)
So §3B is live only for the narrow hybrid case — a new-schema document that nonetheless carries the old fit key — and dead for genuine legacy documents. The spec does not say which it means.

